      "Language": "ukr",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The results of the study hemodynamic changes in postprandial period in patients with coronary heart disease (CHD) and chronic pancreatitis (CP). It is established that patients with CHD and HP reduced pumping function of the heart after a meal in patients with isolated CP. In patients with isolated coronary artery disease marked increase in the pumping function of the heart. Reduced pumping function in patients with CP due to reduced end-diastolic index. All three groups are not significant differences in terms of diastolic function. The main differences between groups were found in the subgroup of patients with CP at the time of the survey was in acute phase. It is in this subgroup, a significant decrease not only the pump, but also inotropic cardiac function."},
